"use strict";(self.webpackChunkwoocommerce_multivendor_marketplace_docs=self.webpackChunkwoocommerce_multivendor_marketplace_docs||[]).push([[3344],{51162(e,t,i){i.r(t),i.d(t,{comp:()=>l,data:()=>d});var n=i(20641);const a=i.p+"assets/img/vendor-asktoadmin-list-view.ea32a777.png",s=i.p+"assets/img/vendor-ask-query-modal.3f761e97.png",r=i.p+"assets/img/vendor-asktoadmin-thread-view.3e23c01f.png",o={},l=(0,i(66262).A)(o,[["render",function(e,t){return(0,n.uX)(),(0,n.CE)("div",null,t[0]||(t[0]=[(0,n.Fv)('<h1 id="ask-to-admin" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#ask-to-admin"><span>Ask To Admin</span></a></h1><p>The <strong>Ask To Admin</strong> feature allows vendors to directly communicate with the marketplace admin for queries, clarifications, or support.</p><p>Clear communication between vendors and marketplace administrators is essential for smooth store operations. Whether a vendor needs help with payouts, order processing, commission rates, or account settings, the <strong>Ask To Admin</strong> module provides a dedicated helpdesk system right inside the vendor dashboard.</p><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/vendor-asktoadmin-list-view.png"><img src="'+a+'" alt="Vendor Ask To Admin Dashboard"></a></p><hr><h2 id="ask-to-admin-overview" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#ask-to-admin-overview"><span>Ask To Admin Overview</span></a></h2><ul><li>Vendors can inquire about anything related to the marketplace.</li><li>This option is available in the <strong>vendor dashboard</strong> under <strong>Communication → Ask Admin</strong> (accessible directly at <code>/seller/vendor-asktoadmin/</code>).</li></ul><h3 id="quick-navigation-path" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#quick-navigation-path"><span>Quick Navigation Path</span></a></h3><ol><li>Log into your <strong>Vendor Account</strong>.</li><li>Open the <strong>Seller Dashboard</strong>.</li><li>In the sidebar navigation menu, locate the <strong>Communication</strong> section.</li><li>Click on <strong>Ask Admin</strong>.</li></ol><hr><h2 id="queries-list-management" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#queries-list-management"><span>Queries List Management</span></a></h2><p>The main <strong>Ask Admin</strong> dashboard displays an organized table containing all previous and ongoing inquiries raised by the vendor.</p><h3 id="search-queries-by-subject" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#search-queries-by-subject"><span>Search Queries by Subject</span></a></h3><p>At the top of the table, vendors can use the <strong>Search by subject</strong> input field. Simply type a keyword or subject title and press enter to quickly locate specific past conversations without scrolling through the entire list.</p><h3 id="queries-table-columns" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#queries-table-columns"><span>Queries Table Columns</span></a></h3><table><thead><tr><th style="text-align:left;">Column</th><th style="text-align:left;">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><strong>Date</strong></td><td style="text-align:left;">Displays the date and time when the query was initially created. Click the column heading to sort chronologically in ascending or descending order.</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><strong>Subject</strong></td><td style="text-align:left;">The title of the inquiry submitted by the vendor. Clicking on the subject link opens the full conversation thread.</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><strong>Message</strong></td><td style="text-align:left;">A preview snippet of the initial query text submitted by the vendor.</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><strong>Status</strong></td><td style="text-align:left;">Shows the current resolution state of the query (such as <strong>Open</strong> or <strong>Answered</strong>).</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><strong>Last Reply</strong></td><td style="text-align:left;">Indicates the date and time of the latest reply from either the admin or the vendor. Click to sort queries by latest activity.</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="hint-container tip"><p class="hint-container-title">Quick Access to Query Details</p><p>Vendors can open any query conversation by clicking directly on either the <strong>Date</strong> or the <strong>Subject</strong> link in the table row.</p></div><hr><h2 id="how-vendors-ask-a-query" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#how-vendors-ask-a-query"><span>How Vendors Ask a Query</span></a></h2><ul><li>Navigate to <strong>Ask To Admin</strong> from the vendor dashboard.</li><li>Click on the <strong>Ask Query</strong> button to raise a new query.</li></ul><hr><h2 id="submit-a-query" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#submit-a-query"><span>Submit a Query</span></a></h2><p>When clicking the <strong>Ask Query</strong> button, a clean popup modal appears with the intro message: <em>&quot;Send your question to the store admin and we will get back to you shortly.&quot;</em></p><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/vendor-ask-query-modal.png"><img src="'+s+'" alt="Vendor Ask Query Modal Popup"></a></p><p>Vendors need to fill in two required fields:</p><ol><li><strong>Subject</strong>: Enter a clear, concise title that summarizes your inquiry (e.g., <em>&quot;Payout has not arrived&quot;</em> or <em>&quot;Shipping zone rate inquiry&quot;</em>).</li><li><strong>Message</strong>: Write a detailed explanation of your question or issue. Include helpful details such as order numbers, payout references, or product names so the admin can assist you faster.</li><li>Click on the <strong>Ask</strong> (or <strong>Submit</strong>) button to send the query.</li></ol><div class="hint-container warning"><p class="hint-container-title">Form Validation</p><p>Both <strong>Subject</strong> and <strong>Message</strong> are mandatory. If a vendor attempts to submit an empty form, the system highlights the missing fields with an error message to prevent accidental blank submissions.</p></div><hr><h2 id="admin-notification-threaded-chat" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#admin-notification-threaded-chat"><span>Admin Notification &amp; Threaded Chat</span></a></h2><ul><li>Once the vendor submits the query: <ul><li>The <strong>admin receives an email notification</strong> regarding the vendor’s query.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Threaded &quot;Ask a Question to Admin&quot;</strong>: Vendor and admin replies form a chat-style thread on both the storefront and the admin panel, keeping the conversation history organized and easy to track.</li></ul><hr><h2 id="threaded-conversation-replying-to-queries" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#threaded-conversation-replying-to-queries"><span>Threaded Conversation &amp; Replying to Queries</span></a></h2><p>Clicking on any query from the table opens the dedicated conversation view (<code>?view_query=&lt;query_id&gt;</code>). This interface offers a chat-like messaging experience that keeps the communication history intact.</p><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/vendor-asktoadmin-thread-view.png"><img src="'+r+'" alt="Vendor Ask to Admin Conversation Thread View"></a></p><h3 id="features-of-the-thread-view" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#features-of-the-thread-view"><span>Features of the Thread View</span></a></h3><ol><li><strong>Back Navigation</strong>: Click the <strong>Back</strong> button at the top header to return to the queries list at any time.</li><li><strong>Admin Profile Header</strong>: The top of the thread displays the admin card with the marketplace logo, name (<strong>Admin</strong>), and designated role (<strong>Marketplace Admin</strong>).</li><li><strong>Date Dividers</strong>: Messages are automatically grouped by date dividers (such as <em>September 19, 2026</em>, <em>October 12, 2026</em>) so you can easily follow the timeline of events.</li><li><strong>Chat Bubbles &amp; Role Identification</strong>: <ul><li><strong>Vendor Messages</strong>: Appear on the vendor&#39;s side with your store name, exact time (e.g., <em>8:55 am</em>), and your question.</li><li><strong>Admin Replies</strong>: Appear on the administrator&#39;s side with the Admin label, exact time (e.g., <em>2:20 pm</em>), and the response.</li></ul></li></ol><h3 id="sending-follow-up-replies" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#sending-follow-up-replies"><span>Sending Follow-up Replies</span></a></h3><p>If you need more details or wish to continue the conversation:</p><ol><li>Scroll to the bottom of the conversation thread.</li><li>Locate the <strong>Your Reply</strong> text box with the placeholder <em>&quot;Type your reply...&quot;</em>.</li><li>Type your response or answer to the admin&#39;s question.</li><li>Click the <strong>Send Reply</strong> button.</li><li>Your reply is added immediately to the bottom of the active conversation thread without creating a separate new inquiry.</li></ol><hr><h2 id="query-status-lifecycle" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#query-status-lifecycle"><span>Query Status Lifecycle</span></a></h2><p>The query status gives vendors transparency into the progress of their inquiries:</p><table><thead><tr><th style="text-align:left;">Status</th><th style="text-align:left;">Meaning</th><th style="text-align:left;">Recommended Action</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><span class="wkmp-v2-badge wkmp-v2-badge--warning">Open</span></td><td style="text-align:left;">The query has been submitted and is awaiting administrator review or an ongoing conversation is active.</td><td style="text-align:left;">No action required; wait for admin response or add helpful updates if new information arises.</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><span class="wkmp-v2-badge wkmp-v2-badge--info">Answered</span></td><td style="text-align:left;">The marketplace admin has reviewed the query and posted a reply.</td><td style="text-align:left;">Check the response in the thread. If the issue is solved, no further action is needed; otherwise, reply in the thread.</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><span class="wkmp-v2-badge wkmp-v2-badge--success">Closed / Resolved</span></td><td style="text-align:left;">The inquiry has been fully addressed and completed.</td><td style="text-align:left;">If you encounter a new, unrelated issue, raise a fresh query via <strong>Ask Query</strong>.</td></tr></tbody></table><hr><h2 id="best-practices-for-vendors" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#best-practices-for-vendors"><span>Best Practices for Vendors</span></a></h2><p>To ensure fast and effective responses from the marketplace admin, keep these tips in mind:</p><ul><li><strong>Use Descriptive Subjects</strong>: Instead of generic titles like <em>&quot;Help&quot;</em> or <em>&quot;Issue&quot;</em>, use specific topics like <em>&quot;Tax document request for Order #1042&quot;</em> or <em>&quot;Payout reference clarification&quot;</em>.</li><li><strong>Include Reference Numbers</strong>: Whenever discussing orders, commission discrepancies, or payouts, mention the specific reference numbers or order IDs.</li><li><strong>Keep Discussions in One Thread</strong>: If an issue requires multiple follow-ups, reply inside the existing thread rather than creating multiple separate queries for the same topic.</li><li><strong>Check Spam / Notifications</strong>: Ensure your account email is up to date so you do not miss email alerts when the admin responds.</li></ul><hr><h2 id="benefits" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#benefits"><span>Benefits</span></a></h2><ul><li>Direct communication channel between vendor and admin.</li><li>Helps vendors resolve issues or doubts quickly.</li><li>Improves overall marketplace support and transparency.</li><li>Maintains a clean, permanent audit trail of all questions and solutions for future reference.</li></ul><hr>',51)]))}]]),d=JSON.parse('{"path":"/documentation/ask-to-admin.html","title":"Ask To Admin – Vendor Support & Inquiry Guide","lang":"en-US","frontmatter":{"title":"Ask To Admin – Vendor Support & Inquiry Guide","description":"Complete user guide for vendors to communicate directly with the marketplace admin in WooCommerce Multi-Vendor Marketplace. Learn how to raise queries, search past tickets, and reply in threaded conversations.","head":[["meta",{"name":"keywords","content":"woocommerce marketplace ask to admin, vendor support queries, marketplace vendor inquiry, contact marketplace admin, vendor communication thread, woocommerce multi-vendor helpdesk, vendor admin chat"}],["meta",{"property":"og:title","content":"Ask To Admin – Vendor Support & Inquiry Guide | WooCommerce Multi-Vendor Marketplace"}],["meta",{"property":"og:description","content":"Learn how marketplace vendors submit inquiries, track query statuses, and communicate directly with store administrators using threaded chat in WooCommerce Multi-Vendor Marketplace."}],["meta",{"property":"og:type","content":"article"}]]},"headers":[{"level":2,"title":"Ask To Admin Overview","slug":"ask-to-admin-overview","link":"#ask-to-admin-overview","children":[{"level":3,"title":"Quick Navigation Path","slug":"quick-navigation-path","link":"#quick-navigation-path","children":[]}]},{"level":2,"title":"Queries List Management","slug":"queries-list-management","link":"#queries-list-management","children":[{"level":3,"title":"Search Queries by Subject","slug":"search-queries-by-subject","link":"#search-queries-by-subject","children":[]},{"level":3,"title":"Queries Table Columns","slug":"queries-table-columns","link":"#queries-table-columns","children":[]}]},{"level":2,"title":"How Vendors Ask a Query","slug":"how-vendors-ask-a-query","link":"#how-vendors-ask-a-query","children":[]},{"level":2,"title":"Submit a Query","slug":"submit-a-query","link":"#submit-a-query","children":[]},{"level":2,"title":"Admin Notification & Threaded Chat","slug":"admin-notification-threaded-chat","link":"#admin-notification-threaded-chat","children":[]},{"level":2,"title":"Threaded Conversation & Replying to Queries","slug":"threaded-conversation-replying-to-queries","link":"#threaded-conversation-replying-to-queries","children":[{"level":3,"title":"Features of the Thread View","slug":"features-of-the-thread-view","link":"#features-of-the-thread-view","children":[]},{"level":3,"title":"Sending Follow-up Replies","slug":"sending-follow-up-replies","link":"#sending-follow-up-replies","children":[]}]},{"level":2,"title":"Query Status Lifecycle","slug":"query-status-lifecycle","link":"#query-status-lifecycle","children":[]},{"level":2,"title":"Best Practices for Vendors","slug":"best-practices-for-vendors","link":"#best-practices-for-vendors","children":[]},{"level":2,"title":"Benefits","slug":"benefits","link":"#benefits","children":[]}],"git":{},"filePathRelative":"documentation/ask-to-admin.md"}')}}]);